I left out the two operations additions, because the node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and calling the metadata service would need filesystem and HTTP authority, and the world has no such imports. Either would also send the input's text outside the node. If operations needs them, the graph should grant the node a logging or `http-client` capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(|l| l.trim())
                .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                .map(|l| l.to_string())
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

